---
/**
 * Privacy Policy Page
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/global/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/global/Footer.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'September 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for The Pizza Dough Formula. Learn how we handle your data and protect your privacy."
>
  <Header />

  <main class="flex-grow">
    <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 md:py-16">
      <h1 class="font-heading text-4xl font-bold text-text mb-2">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="text-text-muted mb-8">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <div class="prose prose-lg text-text-muted space-y-6">
        <p class="text-xl leading-relaxed">
          Your privacy matters to us. This policy explains what information we collect,
          how we use it, and your choices regarding your data.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-semibold text-text mt-8 mb-4">Information We Collect</h2>

        <h3 class="font-heading text-xl font-semibold text-text mt-6 mb-3">Calculator Data</h3>
        <p>
          All calculations are performed locally in your browser. We do not store your
          recipes or calculator settings on our servers. The analytics described below
          record a few general choices, such as the pizza style you select, whether a
          pre-ferment is turned on, and whether amounts are shown in grams or ounces.
        </p>

        <h3 class="font-heading text-xl font-semibold text-text mt-6 mb-3">Local Storage</h3>
        <p>
          We use your browser's localStorage to save preferences like:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2">
          <li>Unit preference (grams/ounces)</li>
          <li>Whether you have closed the analytics notice</li>
          <li>Emergency timer state</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          This data stays on your device and is never transmitted to us. The analytics
          identifier described below is also kept in localStorage, but it is sent with
          analytics data.
        </p>

        <h3 class="font-heading text-xl font-semibold text-text mt-6 mb-3">Email Newsletter</h3>
        <p>
          If you sign up for the newsletter, your email address and the time you agreed to
          receive emails are sent through n8n, an automation service. n8n adds them to a Google
          Sheet the site owner keeps, and to Kit, the email service used to send the newsletter.
          The sign-up form below the calculator also sends the name of the pizza style you had
          selected. We use your address only for pizza tips and site updates.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Every newsletter email includes an unsubscribe link. You can also email
          <a href="mailto:admin@thedoughformula.com" class="text-primary hover:underline">admin@thedoughformula.com</a>
          to be removed from both the mailing list and the spreadsheet.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <strong>Data retention:</strong> Email addresses are kept until you ask for them
          to be removed.
        </p>

        <h3 class="font-heading text-xl font-semibold text-text mt-6 mb-3">Analytics</h3>
        <p>
          We use PostHog to understand how the site is used. PostHog does not set cookies on
          this site. It keeps one randomly generated identifier in your browser's localStorage,
          so the pages you view are counted as one visitor instead of a new visitor on every
          page. The identifier stays until you clear your browser's data for this site, so a
          later visit from the same browser is recognized too.
        </p>
        <p>PostHog records:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2">
          <li>Pages viewed and the page you arrived from</li>
          <li>Actions on the site, such as copying, printing, or sharing a recipe, the pizza style selected, and clicks on equipment links</li>
          <li>Recordings of how pages are used, such as scrolling and clicks. Everything typed into form fields is hidden in these recordings. Text shown on the page, including calculated recipe amounts, is visible.</li>
          <li>Reports of script errors, so we can find and fix problems</li>
          <li>Browser type, device type, screen size, and an approximate location based on your IP address</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Analytics does not collect your name or email address. If your browser sends a
          Do Not Track signal, analytics does not load.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-semibold text-text mt-8 mb-4">Cookies and Local Storage</h2>
        <p>
          This site does not use cookies for analytics or advertising. The table below lists
          what the site keeps in your browser's localStorage.
        </p>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto mt-4">
          <table class="w-full text-sm border border-border rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
            <thead class="bg-cream">
              <tr>
                <th class="px-4 py-2 text-left font-semibold text-text">Name</th>
                <th class="px-4 py-2 text-left font-semibold text-text">Purpose</th>
                <th class="px-4 py-2 text-left font-semibold text-text">Duration</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr class="border-t border-border">
                <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">preferredUnit</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-2">Remembers whether you use grams or ounces</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-2">Until you clear site data</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-t border-border bg-cream/30">
                <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">analyticsNoticeDismissed</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-2">Remembers that you closed the analytics notice</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-2">Until you clear site data</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-t border-border">
                <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">emergencyTimer</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-2">Keeps the Emergency dough timer running if you leave the page</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-2">Until the timer is cleared</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-t border-border bg-cream/30">
                <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">ph_[project token]_posthog</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-2">PostHog analytics identifier</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-2">Until you clear site data</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <p class="mt-4">
          You can remove all of these at any time by clearing your browser's data for this site.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-semibold text-text mt-8 mb-4">Third-Party Services</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2">
          <li>
            <strong>PostHog</strong> - Analytics, session recordings, and error reports
            (<a href="https://posthog.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-primary hover:underline">Privacy Policy</a>)
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>n8n</strong> - Sends newsletter sign-ups to the spreadsheet and to Kit
            (<a href="https://n8n.io/legal/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-primary hover:underline">Privacy Policy</a>)
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Kit</strong> - Stores newsletter subscribers and sends the newsletter
            (<a href="https://kit.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-primary hover:underline">Privacy Policy</a>)
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Google</strong> - Google Sheets holds the site owner's copy of the sign-up list
            (<a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-primary hover:underline">Privacy Policy</a>)
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Cloudflare</strong> - Website hosting and CDN
            (<a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-primary hover:underline">Privacy Policy</a>)
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Amazon</strong> - Affiliate product links
            (<a href="https://www.amazon.com/gp/help/customer/display.html?nodeId=468496" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-primary hover:underline">Privacy Policy</a>)
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-semibold text-text mt-8 mb-4">Your Rights</h2>
        <p>You have the right to:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2">
          <li>Request a copy of any personal data we hold about you</li>
          <li>Request deletion of your personal data</li>
          <li>Have your email address removed from the newsletter list by emailing us</li>
          <li>Clear local storage data through your browser settings</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-semibold text-text mt-8 mb-4">Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          This site is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect
          personal information from children.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-semibold text-text mt-8 mb-4">Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this privacy policy from time to time. Significant changes will
          be noted on this page with an updated revision date.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl font-semibold text-text mt-8 mb-4">Contact</h2>
        <p>
          If you have questions about this privacy policy, want to exercise your data rights,
          or request deletion of your data, please contact us at:
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a href="mailto:admin@thedoughformula.com" class="text-primary hover:underline font-medium">
            admin@thedoughformula.com
          </a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
